Climbing Stairs:Write a java program to Count Ways To Reach The N-th Stairs
import java.util.*;
public class Solution{
static final long mod=1000000007;
public static long countDistinctWayToClimbStair(long nStairs){
if(nStairs==0 ||nStairs==1){
return 1;}
long left=1;
long right=1;
for(long i=2;i<=nStairs;i++){
long curr=(left+right)%mod;
left=right;
right=curr;}
return right;
}}
Output:
Input:
5
Output:
8
Time complexity:O(N)
Space complexity:O(1)
Logic:To reach the Nth stair, you can:
	take 1 step from (N-1)th stair
	take 2 steps from (N-2)th stair
So total ways to reach stair N are:
f(n)=f(n-1)+f(n-2)
